note units: sha256 r1
note r1-valid: program validation (1.1): every out-of-range word of AGG and FSM is refused with 2,
note including nonzero unused words, and the boundary values are accepted; then change validation
note and application (1.3: r1chg, r1apply, r1indom, r1alldom). Exit 0 pass, else the failed check's code.
fn aggbase to void
for i ulong 64
put R1P i 0
end
put R1P 0 3544411312749556050
put R1P 1 1
put R1P 2 8
put R1P 3 1
put R1P 4 2
put R1P 5 7
put R1P 6 7
put R1P 7 1
put R1P 8 255
end

fn fsmbase to void
for i ulong 64
put R1P i 0
end
put R1P 0 3544411312749556050
put R1P 1 2
put R1P 2 3
put R1P 3 4
put R1P 4 0
put R1P 5 3
put R1P 6 10
put R1P 7 20
put R1P 8 30
put R1P 22 16908544
put R1P 23 33751040
put R1P 24 197377
end

note word w = v on the base program (fam 1 AGG, 2 FSM) is refused, and the base itself is valid
fn tbad fam ulong w ulong v ulong to bool
if eq fam 1
aggbase
else
fsmbase
end
if ne r1valid 0
ret false
end
put R1P w v
ret eq r1valid 2
end

fn tgood fam ulong w ulong v ulong to bool
if eq fam 1
aggbase
else
fsmbase
end
put R1P w v
ret eq r1valid 0
end

